# =============================================================================
# RSG Guard Terminal - environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and adjust as needed.
# Expo only inlines variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ at build time, so the
# app reads EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL only (see mobile/src/config.ts).
#
# The backend listens on PORT 4000 (no /api prefix), Swagger at /api-docs.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API base URL resolution order (mobile/src/config.ts):
#
#   a. If EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is set and non-empty, it is used verbatim.
#   b. Otherwise, on a REAL DEVICE running a dev build, the app derives the
#      PC LAN IP from the dev server (Constants.expoConfig.hostUri, e.g.
#      "192.168.1.5:8081") and uses http://<that-ip>:4000.
#   c. Otherwise, on an ANDROID EMULATOR it uses http://10.0.2.2:4000
#      (10.0.2.2 maps to the host machine's localhost). The iOS Simulator /
#      web use http://127.0.0.1:4000.
#
# --- Case 1: Android emulator (no override needed) ----------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
#
# --- Case 2: Real phone over Wi-Fi (auto-detected from the dev server) --------
# Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL unset and run `npx expo start`; the app picks up
# the bundler's LAN IP automatically. Set it only if auto-detection fails or
# for a standalone/release build with no dev server:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.50:4000
#
# --- Case 3: Custom / remote / tunnelled backend ------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:4000   # force emulator host

# =============================================================================
# Windows firewall - allow inbound to the backend on port 4000
# =============================================================================
# Run in an ELEVATED PowerShell so other devices on the LAN can reach the API:
#
#   netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="RSG Backend 4000" dir=in action=allow protocol=TCP localport=4000
#
# Remove it later:
#   netsh advfirewall firewall delete rule name="RSG Backend 4000"

# =============================================================================
# Android cleartext HTTP (development)
# =============================================================================
# Expo Go and debug / dev-client builds already permit cleartext http:// traffic
# in development, so no extra config or rebuild is needed to reach the LAN IP.
# Production / release builds block cleartext by default - for those prefer HTTPS,
# or (not recommended) enable cleartext via the expo-build-properties plugin:
#
#   npm i expo-build-properties
#   # in a dev-only app.config.js:
#   plugins: [["expo-build-properties", { "android": { "usesCleartextTraffic": true } }]]
#
# A prebuild / EAS rebuild IS required for that plugin to take effect.
